"""Every code listing of the SEN0401 chapter 9 deck 2.0.0 (Transaction Fees; a NEW file, the deck 1.1.0 and its examples_v1_0_0.py stay unchanged) and the source of the chapter-code
manifest chapter_code_ch09_v1_0_0.json that the page's chapter-code tab reads. One entry per code slide, in SLIDE ORDER. A listing is a list of GROUPS; a group is a few single-line
statements and the plain-language note that explains them (the deck standard asks for an explanation beside every code box). Every statement is ONE line. The last row of a listing is
an expression (`final`, which is also in `show`): the slide prints its value under it, the only REPL text of the slide; the full result of the example is drawn as a chart or a table beside
the listing from the recorded `show` values (examples_run_v2_0_0.py), never typed. A statement is at most 56 characters, so that a code line never wraps (deck standard D12).
Every example uses only the chapter library of the page (the wheel sen0401_ch09_lib-1.0.2: the module sen0401_ch09_lib_v1_0_1 and the saved records it reads, which the wheel carries).
The values read from R and R2 are the records of two runs of Bitcoin Core 31.1 on regtest (one run each, so they are Recorded on the slides); C is the census of two mainnet blocks;
every other value is computed by the statements."""
__version__ = "2.0.0"

PRELUDE = "import sen0401_ch09_lib_v1_0_1 as L\nR, R2, C = L.run(), L.run2(), L.census()\nB = C['blocks']\n"
G = lambda note, *lines: {"lines": list(lines), "note": note}

